 1. "hello".shout() before anyone defines it           AttributeError
 2. str.shout = shout (a built-in type)                TypeError
 3. setattr(int, "double", double)                     TypeError
 4. Widget.b = f: methods / early.b()                  ['a', 'b'] / 'b'
 5. reassigning Widget.a: early.a() / warning          'a, again' / none
 6. a second class Widget statement -- same class?     False (early.b() still 'b')
 7. class Widget(str) (another base)                   no error; Widget.__mro__[1] is str
 8. object.yell = f                                    TypeError
 9. del Widget.b / delattr(str, "upper")               AttributeError / TypeError
10. class LoudStr(str) -- LoudStr("hello").shout()     'HELLO!!'
